<title>USA: Utah $25 mln housing bonds repriced, restructured.</title>
<headline>Utah $25 mln housing bonds repriced, restructured.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Wednesday it repriced and restructured Utah Housing Finance Agency's $25 million bond deal, lowering the yield in 2016 to 5.65 percent from 5.70 percent and eliminating the 2017 maturity.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>UTAH HOUSING FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $25,000,000*</p>
<p>SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE BONDS</p>
<p>1997 SERIES D</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>NOTE REPRICING FOR THE 2016 SERIES D-1 CLASS I AND DELETION OF</p>
<p>THE 2017 SERIES D-2 MATURITY.</p>
<p>THERE WILL BE A CHANGE ON THE TAXABLE PORTION, BUT IT HAS NOT</p>
<p>BEEN FINALIZED.</p>
<p>NO ADDITIONAL ORDERS WILL BE TAKEN.</p>
<p>					     4,860,000*</p>
